Detailed contracts: KERNEL-PROBES, KERNEL-PROBES-NEXT, COVERAGE-THIRD, MAC-HOOKS.
The JSON inventories and mac-hook-arguments.json identify types and sources.

Original-worktree verification includes 48 first-batch, 34 second-batch and
72 final third-batch kernel compile configurations; enabled/disabled builds,
a linked GENERIC-NODEBUG kernel, native userspace artifacts, and offline
profile compilation. MAC dispatch tests additionally verify argument and skip
semantics. Validation artifacts live under /usr/obj/5bsd-dtrace*-validation
and /usr/obj/5bsd-mac-hook-validation. The isolated commit review records its
checks under /usr/obj/5bsd-tracing-commit-validation.

Isolated branch verification: 154 kernel compile configurations pass with
-Werror against the branch source; all 98 profile checks and both MAC dispatch
fixtures pass. The generated argument contracts match all 336 callback slots
in this branch. Both runtime linkers build and pass ordinary startup, nested
initializers, dlopen/dlclose and missing-library smoke tests. The earlier
SIGSYS limitation in the larger working tree does not reproduce here.

Limits: live DTrace firing remains unqualified because the running host does
not expose the device. No kernel installation, publication or reboot is part
of this change. The commit excludes unrelated loader and MAC policy changes.
